// Title: Renamed Gpg.EXE Execution
// Sigma ID: ec0722a3-eb5c-4a56-8ab2-bf6f20708592
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113
// Date: 2023-08-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: impact, T1486
// Description: Detects the execution of a renamed "gpg.exe". Often used by ransomware and loaders to
//   decrypt/encrypt data.
// References:
//   - https://securelist.com/locked-out/68960/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_gpg4win.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "gpg.exe" and (not((FolderPath endswith "\\gpg.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\gpg2.exe")))
